00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:42,810
Okay.

256
00:15:42,893 --> 00:15:44,040
You can call me a beater.

257
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:48,300
Just make sure you don't confuse
me with those beta testers anymore.

258
00:15:58,840 --> 00:15:59,900
Oh, okay.

259
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:04,217
I didn't know you were the inspiration
for that weird beater handle.

260
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:06,157
Playing the villain was brilliant.

261
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:09,617
By doing that, you took the
heat off the other beta testers.

262
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:12,288
Must have been hard to
take that on, though.

263
00:16:12,660 --> 00:16:15,200
Nah, it wasn't all that bad.

264
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:18,910
Stacia!

265
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:21,130
Chirico!

266
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,360
Chirico! Sachi!

267
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:45,600
The hard part

268
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:49,520
was making friends and
having to watch them die.

269
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:00,000
Nice job.

270
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:01,497
You getting used to it yet?

271
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:04,060
Yeah, I think I'm getting the hang of it.

272
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:07,657
Still having a hard time opening
my eyes underwater, though.

273
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:09,300
That part's always weird.

274
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,774
But don't worry, you'll get used to it.

275
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,697
Why don't we take a little break now?

276
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:14,610
Roger!

277
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:18,360
It's definitely summer.

278
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,720
It totally is, isn't it?

279
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:24,237
Isn't it supposed to always be
summer in that quest we're going on?

280
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:26,737
Yeah, it's in the southern
part of Soph territory.

281
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:28,677
I heard it gets pretty hot there.

282
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:31,477
I heard it's loaded with
all kinds of new traps.

283
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,390
I can't wait!

284
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:34,777
We better figure out a
way to keep Kirito from

285
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:37,742
going aggro and leaving
us all in the dust again.

286
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:41,042
Hey, I've been meaning to
ask you guys something.

287
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:45,044
When you were stuck in the game,
how did you all meet my brother?

288
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:48,877
I was surrounded by a
bunch of monsters and he

289
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:51,607
saved me just as I was
about to get attacked.

290
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:08,580
Pina! Pina! Pina!

291
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:10,930
Pina!

292
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:13,930
Pina!

293
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:21,520
Head!

294
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:52,160
Oh, my God.

295
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:56,390
Peter...

296
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,261
Why would you do all this for me?

297
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:05,772
I'll tell you, but only if you
promise not to laugh, okay?

298
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:07,980
I promise I won't.

299
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:11,550
All right.

300
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:14,468
It's because you look
like my little sister.

301
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:23,200
I'm sorry.

302
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:31,180
Only Kirito would say
something as goofy as that.

303
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:36,680
I mean, compared to you, Suguha,
Keiko doesn't look a thing like you.

304
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:40,022
What about us are you comparing?

305
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:49,247
Anyway, after that, Kirito took me on a
quest to find a rare item to save Pina.

306
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:09,100
Go ahead, pick it up.

307
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:18,920
You sure it'll bring Pina
back to life? Uh-huh.

308
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:20,480
I'm so glad.

309
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:23,617
There's a bunch of strong
monsters lurking around here.

310
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:25,657
Let's revive it when we get back to town.

311
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:27,916
I'm sure Pina would want it that way.

312
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:31,100
Calm down!

313
00:20:31,380 --> 00:20:33,086
That thing's not that strong!

314
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:36,420
Help you! Don't save me!
But don't look! Save me!

315
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:37,350
But don't look!

316
00:20:37,433 --> 00:20:39,340
That'll be... difficult. Help me down!

317
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:41,360
No! No!

318
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:50,340
Do you see anything?

319
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:53,997
When I first met your brother,

320
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:57,256
it wasn't half as dramatic
as what happened to Silica.

321
00:20:58,740 --> 00:21:00,916
Welcome to Lizbeth's blacksmith shop.

322
00:21:02,020 --> 00:21:03,280
Oh, hi.

323
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:06,133
I was wondering if you do custom orders.

324
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:13,068
He doesn't look like
he has that much money.

325
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:14,790
I can.

326
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:17,857
The thing is, metal prices
are kind of high these days.

327
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:20,277
Oh, well, I'm not worried about the cost.

328
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:23,137
I just want the best sword you
can make as soon as possible.

329
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:25,157
Well, I make a lot of different swords,

330
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:28,697
but if you have any idea of the quality
of swords you want, I can make it.

331
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:30,060
Uh, sure. One sec.

332
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:35,560
So, I'm looking for something either the
same quality or better than this. Oh.

333
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:40,370
An elucidator!

334
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,710
monster drop.

335
00:21:49,793 --> 00:21:50,623
What do you think?

336
00:21:50,706 --> 00:21:51,680
How about this?

337
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,637
It's the best sword I ever forged.

338
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:54,550
I call it my

339
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:57,150
masterpiece.

340
00:21:57,233 --> 00:21:58,063
I don't know.

341
00:21:58,146 --> 00:21:58,976
It's a little light.

342
00:21:59,059 --> 00:21:59,889
It should be.

343
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:02,315
I used a speed type metal to forge it.

344
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:05,560
I'd like to test it if
it's cool. Test it how?

345
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:07,549
You know, it's durability.

346
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:10,917
What the heck are you doing?

347
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,057
If you break your sword,
I'm not responsible.

348
00:22:13,140 --> 00:22:15,140
If it breaks, then that's too bad!

349
00:22:26,420 --> 00:22:29,140
He just walked in and
destroyed my best sword.

350
00:22:29,580 --> 00:22:31,580
Talk about a bad first impression.

351
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:33,320
I'm sorry about that.

352
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,597
That's how he is, though.

353
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:37,860
Always doing the one thing
you'd least expect. Yeah,

354
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:40,217
like the time we fell into
a dragon's lair and he

355
00:22:40,300 --> 00:22:43,037
handed me a pile of its poop
like it was no big deal.

356
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:44,677
Definitely not a good memory.

357
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,860
I'm with you there, Liz. No.

358
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:50,233
Actually, there were some good memories.

359
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:00,740
It's so warm.

360
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:02,090
Huh?

361
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:07,555
Even though you and me are just these
ones and zeros in a virtual world.

362
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,050
I know.

363
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:16,860
Look at that!

364
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:28,570
Kirito!

365
00:23:29,120 --> 00:23:30,277
You know what?

366
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:31,920
No, what?

367
00:23:32,820 --> 00:23:33,980
Don't freak out!

368
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:36,200
But I'm falling in love with you!

369
00:23:37,460 --> 00:23:39,080
I can't hear a thing!

370
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:40,674
What did you just say?

371
00:23:42,520 --> 00:23:43,640
Never mind!

372
00:23:52,520 --> 00:23:53,980
Do me a favor, okay?

373
00:23:54,460 --> 00:23:56,107
Tell Asuna what you told me.

374
00:23:56,740 --> 00:23:57,570
Liz...

375
00:23:57,653 --> 00:23:58,620
I'm fine, really.

376
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:03,040
The getting over it part,
that's gonna take a while.

377
00:24:04,660 --> 00:24:06,540
Until I do, promise me.

378
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,529
Promise me you'll put
an end to this world.

379
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:14,580
Till then, I'll keep doing what I do best.

380
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:17,680
I don't know.

381
00:24:19,540 --> 00:24:20,420
Damn him.

382
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:24,295
I bet he's flirting with that
cute counselor right now.

383
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:28,480
You see that? Right there. What? Where?

384
00:24:28,620 --> 00:24:29,700
Right there, see?

385
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:31,137
What am I looking at?

386
00:24:31,220 --> 00:24:32,691
Those coordinates, there.

387
00:24:33,220 --> 00:24:37,691
I see a boss raid, all the high-level
players, and who do you think that is?

388
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:39,360
I thought so.

389
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:42,457
There you are, the strongest
solo player in the game,

390
00:24:42,540 --> 00:24:44,557
joining a raid party to fight a boss.

391
00:24:44,640 --> 00:24:47,457
I'm sure you understand why I
was surprised to see you there.

392
00:24:47,540 --> 00:24:48,893
Well, you shouldn't be.

393
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:52,922
With four bosses, being a high-level
solo player didn't mean jack.

394
00:24:53,340 --> 00:24:54,320
You needed help.

395
00:24:54,620 --> 00:24:58,057
There were bosses that posed a
threat, even if you were in a party.

396
00:24:58,140 --> 00:25:01,320
Like Illfang the Kobold
Lord, the floor wand boss.

397
00:25:01,580 --> 00:25:04,286
His level was so high,
he almost wiped us out.

398
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,400
Diago, no!

399
00:25:23,340 --> 00:25:24,180
Watch out!

400
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,660
You're going down!

401
00:25:41,580 --> 00:25:44,500
There was Gleam Eyes,
the boss on floor 74.

402
00:25:45,060 --> 00:25:47,440
I beat it using my dual-wielding skill.

403
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:51,407
But I came this close to getting
myself killed in the process.

404
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:08,400
Okay, here goes.

405
00:26:09,080 --> 00:26:10,400
Starburst stream!

406
00:26:18,140 --> 00:26:20,260
What the hell kind of skill is that?

407
00:26:21,260 --> 00:26:22,090
Faster!

408
00:26:31,260 --> 00:26:33,100
Gotta go faster!

409
00:27:01,500 --> 00:27:03,206
And that was just the bosses.

410
00:27:03,560 --> 00:27:06,117
But in Aincrad, there was
something even scarier.

411
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:07,030
Yeah?

412
00:27:07,113 --> 00:27:07,943
What was that?

413
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:09,340
The other players.

414
00:27:10,020 --> 00:27:10,850
Seriously?

415
00:27:11,740 --> 00:27:12,570
Yeah.

416
00:27:12,653 --> 00:27:14,197
The bosses' parameters were intimidating.

417
00:27:14,280 --> 00:27:16,633
But in the end, they were just programs.

418
00:27:16,820 --> 00:27:20,217
Once you figured out their attack
patterns, you could deal with them.

419
00:27:20,300 --> 00:27:23,377
And since they couldn't leave their
dungeons, you could always bail.

420
00:27:23,460 --> 00:27:26,357
But players, red players, were human too.

421
00:27:26,440 --> 00:27:29,675
And they were always coming
up with new ways to PK you.

422
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:31,682
And they killed lots of players.

423
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:52,856
We've been poisoned.

424
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:13,280
Why do you keep struggling?

425
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:15,600
Are you afraid of dying after all?

426
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:19,840
No, I'm just not ready yet.

427
00:28:20,940 --> 00:28:22,380
Is that so?

428
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:25,540
That's the way I like it!

429
00:28:37,440 --> 00:28:39,000
Die! Die! Die!

430
00:28:42,260 --> 00:28:45,157
It wasn't just the fights
with red players, either.

431
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:48,920
I found myself in hairy situations
and straight up duels, too.

432
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:54,106
We may be the top guild, but we barely
get by with the amount of troops we have.

433
00:29:06,500 --> 00:29:07,940
His shield?

434
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:22,620
Your reaction time is very impressive.

435
00:29:35,580 --> 00:29:36,960
Now's my chance!

436
00:29:58,360 --> 00:30:01,717
Right, Heathcliff, the leader of
the Knights of the Blood Oath.

437
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:04,918
He was brilliant, one of
the top players in the game.

438
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:07,480
Yeah, and what's ironic is,

439
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:11,661
it was my duel with him that tipped
me off about his true identity.

440
00:30:14,440 --> 00:30:18,220
I made a little something for
everyone, so dig in! No way!

441
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:21,437
Um, I brought along
some lunch to share too.

442
00:30:21,520 --> 00:30:23,755
Help yourselves, do whatever you want.

443
00:30:24,200 --> 00:30:25,440
Thanks for the food!

444
00:30:32,420 --> 00:30:33,250
Who's it from?

445
00:30:33,940 --> 00:30:34,770
Kirito.

446
00:30:34,853 --> 00:30:36,286
He says to start without him.

447
00:30:37,180 --> 00:30:38,010
Okay, then.

448
00:30:38,180 --> 00:30:41,004
I'll just put Kirito's
share in my stomach, too.

449
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:42,717
You can't eat up all his food.

450
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:43,630
That's mean.

451
00:30:43,713 --> 00:30:45,497
We have to leave some for him, too.

452
00:30:45,580 --> 00:30:46,410
Okay.

453
00:30:49,300 --> 00:30:50,130
Wow.

454
00:30:50,213 --> 00:30:51,446
Asuna's lunch is so adorable.

455
00:30:52,260 --> 00:30:55,180
I wonder if that's the
kind of girl Kazuto likes.

456
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:58,616
It's the kind that are all
feminine and can cook good.

457
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:02,860
Is something wrong,
Suguha? Huh? Oh, nothing.

458
00:31:03,120 --> 00:31:06,355
I was just wondering how you
and my brother met at all.

459
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:08,257
He never told me, so...

460
00:31:08,340 --> 00:31:11,300
Yeah, tell us how you guys met. Really?

461
00:31:11,700 --> 00:31:12,680
Oh, come on.

462
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:14,817
We just told you, so it's only fair.

463
00:31:14,900 --> 00:31:15,730
She's right.

464
00:31:15,813 --> 00:31:18,934
You're the only one here who
hasn't talked about it yet.

465
00:31:20,080 --> 00:31:22,900
Well, since you put it
that way... Yeah, right!

466
00:31:24,860 --> 00:31:27,900
So, we first met in a town called Tolbana.

467
00:31:28,260 --> 00:31:32,613
It was on floor one at a boss raid
meeting, and I sort of brushed him off.

468
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:36,671
At the time, all I could think
about was clearing the game.

469
00:31:38,420 --> 00:31:40,980
You really think these taste good? Uh-huh.

470
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:45,757
Since I came to this town, I end
up eating at least one a day.

471
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:48,497
Of course, I got a trick
to make it taste better.

472
00:31:48,580 --> 00:31:49,410
What trick?

473
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:53,131
Try it with some of that.

474
00:32:04,720 --> 00:32:05,550
Cream?

475
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:32,337
He taught me that even though
we were stuck in Aincrad,

476
00:32:32,420 --> 00:32:34,714
we could still find ways to enjoy life.

477
00:32:40,220 --> 00:32:42,060
Oh, hey. What's up?

478
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:46,037
Everyone in the assault team's working
their butts off to clear the dungeon.

479
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:47,532
And where do I find you?

480
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:49,140
Out here, taking a nap.

481
00:32:49,580 --> 00:32:52,117
Even if you're a solo player,
you should take this more soon.

482
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:55,017
Bet you didn't know this
is Aincrad's nicest season.

483
00:32:55,100 --> 00:32:57,437
Today's weather is at its optimal setting.

484
00:32:57,520 --> 00:32:58,350
Huh?

485
00:32:58,433 --> 00:33:01,457
It'd be a waste to have to go
to work on a day like this.

486
00:33:01,540 --> 00:33:02,370
Whatever.

487
00:33:02,453 --> 00:33:03,597
I can't believe you.

488
00:33:03,680 --> 00:33:05,974
Do you even understand what's going on?

489
00:33:06,180 --> 00:33:09,197
Every day here is another
one lost in the real world.

490
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:12,197
Yeah, but right now, we're
not in the real world, are we?

491
00:33:12,280 --> 00:33:13,660
We're alive in Aincrad.

492
00:33:17,620 --> 00:33:18,450
See?

493
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:20,405
Doesn't that breeze feel good?

494
00:33:20,700 --> 00:33:21,720
And the sun.

495
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:22,980
Oh, come on.

496
00:33:23,280 --> 00:33:25,339
The weather's always the same here.

497
00:33:26,600 --> 00:33:30,424
If you laid down on the grass for
a little bit, you'd understand.

498
00:33:58,060 --> 00:34:00,860
Oh, my God.

499
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:07,840
Oh, damn.

500
00:34:07,960 --> 00:34:08,790
Would you look at that.

501
00:34:08,873 --> 00:34:10,517
Taking a nap in the middle of the day.

502
00:34:10,600 --> 00:34:12,177
Some people sure got it easy.

503
00:34:12,260 --> 00:34:14,200
Couple of lazy losers, man.

504
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:18,180
I can't believe she fell asleep.

505
00:34:49,840 --> 00:34:50,820
Good morning.

506
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:52,694
You slept like a rock.

507
00:34:58,480 --> 00:35:00,160
You get one meal.

508
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:02,720
One meal.

509
00:35:03,680 --> 00:35:05,209
All you can eat, my treat.

510
00:35:05,600 --> 00:35:07,300
Then we'll be even. Deal?

511
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:12,757
If everything happened
the way you just said,

512
00:35:12,840 --> 00:35:16,077
then it sounds like you fell for
Kitty till before he fell for you.

513
00:35:16,160 --> 00:35:17,917
N-No, it wasn't like...

514
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,380
Uh, don't deny it.

515
00:35:19,540 --> 00:35:21,897
Remember when you came to
get your sword sharpened?

516
00:35:21,980 --> 00:35:25,274
You were all sad because you
thought he wasn't into you.

517
00:35:25,880 --> 00:35:27,137
So how'd you snag him?

518
00:35:27,220 --> 00:35:30,077
Did you chase him down
and confess your feelings?

519
00:35:30,160 --> 00:35:30,990
Well...

520
00:35:32,320 --> 00:35:34,520
So, where am I going to cook it?

521
00:35:35,220 --> 00:35:36,677
Oh, well...

522
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:38,777
I'm guessing not your place, right?

523
00:35:38,860 --> 00:35:40,389
You even own any cookware?

524
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:42,750
Okay,

525
00:35:42,833 --> 00:35:44,777
because the main ingredient is special,

526
00:35:44,860 --> 00:35:47,978
I won't have a problem if
we used my place this time.

527
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:50,430
Good.

528
00:35:51,980 --> 00:35:54,627
So, what do you say you
and me team up again?

529
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:58,077
Black's my lucky color this week anyway.

530
00:35:58,160 --> 00:35:58,990
Hold up a sec.

531
00:35:59,073 --> 00:36:01,297
Don't you have stuff you
have to do for your guild?

532
00:36:01,380 --> 00:36:02,557
You can't just bail on him.

533
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:05,057
It's not like we have any
leveling quotas to meet.

534
00:36:05,140 --> 00:36:06,897
Well, then what about your bodyguard?

535
00:36:06,980 --> 00:36:08,156
I'll just ditch him.

536
00:36:32,200 --> 00:36:34,435
The front lines are dangerous, though.

537
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:40,920
Okay, fine.

538
00:36:46,980 --> 00:36:50,197
Whoa, I didn't think you'd
be that aggressive about it.

539
00:36:50,280 --> 00:36:53,957
Maybe you have to be that aggressive
to get a guy to pay attention.

540
00:36:54,040 --> 00:36:55,660
What could I do?

541
00:36:55,980 --> 00:36:58,860
After all, I was in love with him.

542
00:36:59,560 --> 00:37:02,057
Aw, that's the sweetest
thing I've ever heard.

543
00:37:02,140 --> 00:37:04,360
So, how far'd you guys go, huh?

544
00:37:04,620 --> 00:37:07,537
I know it was in-game, but
you weren't married, so...

545
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:08,450
Did you?

546
00:37:08,533 --> 00:37:09,363
Or did you?

547
00:37:13,060 --> 00:37:14,040
I'm sorry.

548
00:37:14,980 --> 00:37:15,937
This was...

549
00:37:16,020 --> 00:37:18,480
all my fault, wasn't it?

550
00:37:26,220 --> 00:37:27,050
Asuna...

551
00:37:27,133 --> 00:37:28,120
I'm sorry.

552
00:37:29,040 --> 00:37:30,257
But I...

553
00:37:30,340 --> 00:37:32,237
I should...

554
00:37:32,320 --> 00:37:34,020
stay away from you.

555
00:37:37,920 --> 00:37:39,780
For your sake.

556
00:37:59,060 --> 00:38:01,197
Asuna, my life belongs to you.

557
00:38:01,280 --> 00:38:03,037
I'll give it up for you!

558
00:38:03,120 --> 00:38:05,800
I want to stay with you until the end.

559
00:38:07,780 --> 00:38:12,737
And I promise I'll do anything
to protect you, too. Forever.

560
00:38:12,820 --> 00:38:13,937
No matter what.

561
00:38:14,020 --> 00:38:15,040
I swear.

562
00:38:15,420 --> 00:38:20,360
I'll do everything I can to make
sure you get back to the real world.

563
00:38:22,700 --> 00:38:27,480
Asuna, could I stay
with you for the night?

564
00:38:54,920 --> 00:38:55,920
Don't look.

565
00:38:56,720 --> 00:38:58,060
Not yet, anyway.

566
00:39:01,720 --> 00:39:03,191
What are you waiting for?

567
00:39:03,340 --> 00:39:04,170
Get undressed.

568
00:39:04,560 --> 00:39:06,277
Don't just sit there.

569
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:07,520
It's embarrassing.

570
00:39:23,700 --> 00:39:25,980
Hey, what are you smiling about?

571
00:39:27,740 --> 00:39:32,020
I was just having a
dream about my old life.

572
00:39:34,120 --> 00:39:38,500
It was weird, and the dream
I had, everything in Aincrad,

573
00:39:38,880 --> 00:39:43,900
everything that happened in meeting you was
just that, a dream, and I was so scared,

574
00:39:44,300 --> 00:39:45,580
but it wasn't.

575
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,440
Thank God it wasn't.

576
00:39:47,600 --> 00:39:49,040
Now that sounds weird.

577
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,097
Don't you want to go back?

578
00:39:51,180 --> 00:39:52,340
Of course I do.

579
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:56,800
I do, it's just, I don't want my
life here to disappear is all.

580
00:39:57,500 --> 00:40:00,077
The last two years have
been very special to me.

581
00:40:00,160 --> 00:40:02,160
I realize that now.

582
00:40:07,080 --> 00:40:12,240
Listen, Kirito, I was thinking, maybe we
could leave the front lines for a while.

583
00:40:12,600 --> 00:40:13,430
What?

584
00:40:15,080 --> 00:40:16,080
I'm scared.

585
00:40:16,500 --> 00:40:21,441
I feel like if we return to the battlefield
now, something bad's gonna happen again.

586
00:40:21,660 --> 00:40:23,700
Or maybe I'm just tired of it all.

587
00:40:25,220 --> 00:40:26,560
I know what you mean.

588
00:40:26,960 --> 00:40:28,940
I guess I am too.

589
00:40:32,180 --> 00:40:34,360
In the southwest of Floor 22,

590
00:40:34,680 --> 00:40:38,300
there's this tiny little
village by a lake and a forest.

591
00:40:39,180 --> 00:40:43,140
We could get a house together, and then...

592
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:44,590
And then what?

593
00:40:47,560 --> 00:40:48,390
Then...

594
00:40:49,340 --> 00:40:50,560
We get married.

595
00:41:01,260 --> 00:41:02,090
Okay.

596
00:41:05,340 --> 00:41:06,760
Hello, Earthda Asuna.

597
00:41:08,040 --> 00:41:08,940
Huh? Nothing!

598
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:10,357
I mean, we didn't!

599
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:11,937
I mean, we didn't do anything!

600
00:41:12,020 --> 00:41:13,340
Man, I'm so jealous.

601
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:18,020
You're so lucky being all married
and having Yui, the cutest kid ever.

602
00:41:18,500 --> 00:41:19,740
She is great.

603
00:41:19,940 --> 00:41:22,040
Our pride and joy. Look at you.

604
00:41:22,220 --> 00:41:24,926
You're quite the doting
parent for a teenager.

605
00:41:25,060 --> 00:41:27,884
I think I'll take that
as a compliment, Smartie.

606
00:41:28,860 --> 00:41:33,625
Seriously, we want to make Yui happy, too,
so we'll do our best on today's quest.

607
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:40,440
A-una-ki-to?

608
00:41:41,480 --> 00:41:42,700
Try to remember.

609
00:41:43,100 --> 00:41:45,100
What were you doing in the forest?

610
00:41:45,360 --> 00:41:48,125
And do you know where
your mom and dad are now?

611
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:52,100
I don't know.

612
00:41:53,220 --> 00:41:55,780
They can't remember anything.

613
00:41:57,340 --> 00:41:58,170
Oh, no.

614
00:42:00,520 --> 00:42:02,280
Well, you're awake.

615
00:42:04,520 --> 00:42:05,960
Can I call you, Yui?

616
00:42:06,780 --> 00:42:07,610
Mm-hmm.

617
00:42:08,160 --> 00:42:08,990
Okay.

618
00:42:09,073 --> 00:42:10,447
Then you can call me Kirito.

619
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:12,040
Can you say Kirito?

620
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:14,830
Kirito.

621
00:42:15,120 --> 00:42:16,040
It's Kirito.

622
00:42:16,940 --> 00:42:17,770
Kirito.

623
00:42:21,220 --> 00:42:22,050
Kirito.

624
00:42:23,080 --> 00:42:23,960
That's okay.

625
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:25,057
Maybe it's a little hard.

626
00:42:25,140 --> 00:42:28,160
How about you call me
whatever's easier for you?

627
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:31,620
Daddy.

628
00:42:32,480 --> 00:42:33,310
Me?

629
00:42:35,460 --> 00:42:36,360
Oh, nice.

630
00:42:37,220 --> 00:42:38,050
Mommy.

631
00:42:44,420 --> 00:42:45,560
Okay.

632
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:48,100
I'm Mommy. That works.

633
00:42:49,320 --> 00:42:50,220
Mommy!

634
00:42:51,140 --> 00:42:52,797
Mommy! Daddy!

635
00:42:52,880 --> 00:42:55,460
You must be hungry.

636
00:42:55,800 --> 00:42:57,057
Now, what about breakfast?

637
00:42:57,140 --> 00:42:57,970
Okay.

638
00:43:01,300 --> 00:43:03,280
Yui? Yui.

639
00:43:04,360 --> 00:43:05,240
Daddy.

640
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:06,830
Mommy.

641
00:43:07,440 --> 00:43:08,420
Don't worry.

642
00:43:08,720 --> 00:43:10,014
I remember everything.

643
00:43:12,160 --> 00:43:15,400
Mental Health Counseling
Program Prototype 1.

644
00:43:15,900 --> 00:43:17,140
Codename Yui.

645
00:43:18,060 --> 00:43:19,800
That is who I am.

646
00:43:23,980 --> 00:43:26,156
You aren't just some program anymore.

647
00:43:26,420 --> 00:43:28,126
The system can't control you.

648
00:43:28,300 --> 00:43:31,829
Listen, if you want something,
all you have to do is say it.

649
00:43:32,620 --> 00:43:34,502
Go ahead, tell us what you want.

650
00:43:37,500 --> 00:43:39,300
What I want...

651
00:43:41,580 --> 00:43:42,620
I want...

652
00:43:46,040 --> 00:43:48,180
I want to stay with you forever!

653
00:43:50,040 --> 00:43:51,180
Daddy! Mommy!

654
00:43:57,860 --> 00:43:59,260
You will.

655
00:43:59,660 --> 00:44:01,820
We'll be together forever, Yui.

656
00:44:03,400 --> 00:44:04,300
Yeah.

657
00:44:04,800 --> 00:44:06,500
Remember, you're our child.

658
00:44:15,180 --> 00:44:16,680
Are you okay?

659
00:44:22,900 --> 00:44:23,900
What's this?

660
00:44:24,480 --> 00:44:27,715
The system was about to reject
Yui's admin credentials.

661
00:44:28,060 --> 00:44:32,648
The only thing I could do was take her
program and turn it into a game object.

662
00:44:33,200 --> 00:44:35,477
So this is...

663
00:44:35,560 --> 00:44:38,000
You're holding Yui's heart.

664
00:44:48,780 --> 00:44:49,657
That's amazing.

665
00:44:49,740 --> 00:44:53,260
He never told me about
how you met Yui in SAO?

666
00:44:54,700 --> 00:44:55,777
That's how it happened.

667
00:44:55,860 --> 00:44:58,360
And ever since then, she's been our child.

668
00:45:00,900 --> 00:45:01,730
Okay.

669
00:45:01,813 --> 00:45:03,937
Let's get back in the pool
and practice some more!

670
00:45:04,020 --> 00:45:05,497
Come on, Shiguha.

671
00:45:05,580 --> 00:45:09,237
A couple more lessons and you'll
be swimming circles around Kirito.

672
00:45:09,320 --> 00:45:10,150
Cool.

673
00:45:13,440 --> 00:45:15,322
It's good to be young, isn't it?

674
00:45:15,780 --> 00:45:19,837
I hope those girls realize how lucky
they are to be back in the real world.

675
00:45:19,920 --> 00:45:22,937
They'd be dead if it weren't
for your heroic actions.

676
00:45:23,020 --> 00:45:24,760
I wasn't trying to be a hero.

677
00:45:25,140 --> 00:45:28,317
You figured out Heathcliff was
Akihiko Kayaba, didn't you?

678
00:45:28,400 --> 00:45:32,694
If beating him at his own game wasn't
a heroic act, I don't know what is.

679
00:45:33,060 --> 00:45:35,589
It didn't seem like it
at the time, though.

680
00:45:54,020 --> 00:45:55,900
I'm sorry, Asuna.

681
00:45:56,380 --> 00:45:58,520
Please, keep living.

682
00:46:09,360 --> 00:46:11,500
Game over, Kirito.

683
00:46:36,220 --> 00:46:37,537
Asuna...

684
00:46:37,620 --> 00:46:38,877
Asuna...

685
00:46:38,960 --> 00:46:40,177
You can't...

686
00:46:40,260 --> 00:46:41,580
You can't be...

687
00:46:46,020 --> 00:46:47,900
I'm sorry.

688
00:46:49,500 --> 00:46:50,900
Goodbye.

689
00:47:33,980 --> 00:47:34,810
It's...

690
00:47:34,893 --> 00:47:35,723
It's...

691
00:47:35,806 --> 00:47:36,636
over now.

692
00:47:41,380 --> 00:47:43,200
I believe in you, Kirito.

693
00:47:59,580 --> 00:48:00,410
Not yet.

694
00:48:08,020 --> 00:48:09,040
Not yet.

695
00:48:20,480 --> 00:48:21,310
We did it.

696
00:48:34,680 --> 00:48:35,660
Didn't we?

697
00:49:10,920 --> 00:49:15,140
On November 7th at 2.55pm,
the game has been cleared.

698
00:49:15,660 --> 00:49:18,100
Repeat, the game has been cleared.

699
00:49:21,120 --> 00:49:24,917
The report states that after Kayaba
lost the final battle with you,

700
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:28,037
his brain was fried instantly
by his nerve gear rig.

701
00:49:28,120 --> 00:49:30,440
The autopsy on him confirmed as much.

702
00:49:31,500 --> 00:49:34,340
However, there's one
thing that puzzles me.

703
00:49:34,680 --> 00:49:38,660
You were killed in-game before
he was, and yet you survived.

704
00:49:39,540 --> 00:49:44,180
Was that due to a system-related
reason, or was it the will of Kayaba?

705
00:49:47,620 --> 00:49:49,360
A stunning view, isn't it?

706
00:49:59,540 --> 00:50:00,660
Akihiko Kayaba.

707
00:50:01,460 --> 00:50:02,980
At Argus Headquarters,

708
00:50:03,400 --> 00:50:06,857
the SAO mainframe is in a room
five floors below street level,

709
00:50:06,940 --> 00:50:10,293
and right now it's deleting
all the data from its drives.

710
00:50:11,600 --> 00:50:16,000
In about ten minutes, everything in
this world will disappear forever.

711
00:50:17,400 --> 00:50:18,620
And all the players?

712
00:50:18,960 --> 00:50:20,260
What happens to them?

713
00:50:21,400 --> 00:50:23,459
You don't have to worry about them.

714
00:50:23,840 --> 00:50:30,260
The 6,147 players who survived the game up
to now were logged out a few seconds ago.

715
00:50:31,720 --> 00:50:34,680
And what about the 4,000 people who died?

716
00:50:35,140 --> 00:50:36,380
What about them?

717
00:50:37,580 --> 00:50:38,860
They'll never return.

718
00:50:39,360 --> 00:50:43,480
In any world, real or virtual,
once you're dead, you're gone.

719
00:50:47,400 --> 00:50:48,230
Why?

720
00:50:48,313 --> 00:50:49,143
What's the point?

721
00:50:49,340 --> 00:50:50,600
Why did you do this?

722
00:50:51,820 --> 00:50:53,417
That's a good question.

723
00:50:53,500 --> 00:50:56,088
It's been so long I've
forgotten the reason.

724
00:50:57,240 --> 00:50:58,480
Isn't that strange?

725
00:50:59,520 --> 00:51:04,344
Even before I developed a system for the
full-dive environment, I dreamed of this.

726
00:51:04,720 --> 00:51:09,180
A castle in a world that wasn't governed
by earthly laws and restrictions.

727
00:51:09,800 --> 00:51:12,741
I poured my life into
making that world a reality.

728
00:51:14,940 --> 00:51:16,577
I created this world,

729
00:51:16,660 --> 00:51:21,366
and I got to see something that surpassed
anything I could have imagined for it.

730
00:51:23,660 --> 00:51:27,637
My steel castle floating
in the sky I don't remember

731
00:51:27,720 --> 00:51:31,777
how old I was when I became
obsessed with it I wanted

732
00:51:31,860 --> 00:51:35,897
to leave the earth to fly
to that castle I wanted that

733
00:51:35,980 --> 00:51:39,540
more than anything else for
as long as I can remember

734
00:51:43,680 --> 00:51:50,157
You know what Kirito I want to believe
it's still out there that somewhere in some

735
00:51:50,240 --> 00:51:52,537
other world my castle is still standing

736
00:51:52,620 --> 00:51:58,420
taller than ever Yeah maybe it still is

737
00:52:04,540 --> 00:52:10,600
Before I forget congratulations
on clearing the game Kirito Asuna

738
00:52:14,320 --> 00:52:17,520
Well then I should probably get going now

739
00:52:34,760 --> 00:52:35,780
And that was it?

740
00:52:36,760 --> 00:52:38,797
Kayaba just left you two standing there?

741
00:52:38,880 --> 00:52:42,057
He never gave you a reason
why he made SAO a death game?

742
00:52:42,140 --> 00:52:44,680
Other than that castle story? No.

743
00:52:45,220 --> 00:52:46,338
That's all he said.

744
00:52:54,880 --> 00:52:55,737
Who's that from?

745
00:52:55,820 --> 00:52:58,437
Let me guess—it's from your princess.

746
00:52:58,520 --> 00:53:02,757
When I think of what happened to the
two of you after you survived SAO,

747
00:53:02,840 --> 00:53:04,937
it must have been quite an ordeal.

748
00:53:05,020 --> 00:53:07,377
It was thanks to a certain someone.

749
00:53:07,460 --> 00:53:10,537
A crime was being
committed right inside ALO

750
00:53:10,620 --> 00:53:13,097
and you had no idea it was even happening.

751
00:53:13,180 --> 00:53:16,237
You're right—we dropped the
ball and I'm sorry about that.

752
00:53:16,320 --> 00:53:17,617
It's no excuse.

753
00:53:17,700 --> 00:53:21,657
But by the time we found out what
Nobuyuki Sugo was up to, using those

754
00:53:21,740 --> 00:53:25,420
300 comatose SAO players as
guinea pigs, guinea pigs,

755
00:53:25,740 --> 00:53:28,480
you'd already gone in
and taken care of it.

756
00:53:28,640 --> 00:53:31,397
But why couldn't you stop
him from doing it in the

757
00:53:31,480 --> 00:53:32,310
first place?

758
00:53:32,393 --> 00:53:34,317
It's not like we weren't
keeping tabs on him.

759
00:53:34,400 --> 00:53:36,694
Sugo worked in the same research lab as

760
00:53:37,200 --> 00:53:38,030
Kayaba.

761
00:53:38,113 --> 00:53:41,444
But there were 6,000 players coming
back from SAO that needed us.

762
00:53:41,620 --> 00:53:42,740
We were swamped,

763
00:53:42,860 --> 00:53:46,797
checking up on their health and getting
them adjusted to the real world again.

764
00:53:46,880 --> 00:53:50,762
Our staff was stretched so thin,
monitoring Sugo took a back seat.

765
00:53:51,200 --> 00:53:52,040
That said,

766
00:53:52,300 --> 00:53:54,537
none of us even considered
the possibility of him

767
00:53:54,620 --> 00:53:57,620
building a lab inside the
game for his experiments.

768
00:53:57,920 --> 00:53:59,214
And in the real world,

769
00:54:00,140 --> 00:54:03,037
he gave us no indication he was
involved with anything shady.

770
00:54:03,120 --> 00:54:05,179
Why don't you tell me what happened

771
00:54:05,460 --> 00:54:06,290
in there?

772
00:54:06,373 --> 00:54:09,020
For starters, how do you
know what Sugo was up to?

773
00:54:09,300 --> 00:54:12,300
It's not like I suspected
anything, Not at first.

774
00:54:13,240 --> 00:54:14,070
This is Sugo.

775
00:54:14,153 --> 00:54:16,258
He's our company's director of R &D.

776
00:54:16,640 --> 00:54:18,160
I'm Nobuyuki Sugo.

777
00:54:18,500 --> 00:54:19,441
It's a pleasure.

778
00:54:20,440 --> 00:54:22,380
I'm Kazuto Kirigaya.

779
00:54:24,020 --> 00:54:25,380
Kazuto, take care.

780
00:54:31,360 --> 00:54:34,380
I heard you and Asuna
were lovers in the game.

781
00:54:34,720 --> 00:54:35,720
Is that true?

782
00:54:37,000 --> 00:54:37,830
Uh-huh.

783
00:54:38,340 --> 00:54:39,516
That is unfortunate.

784
00:54:39,880 --> 00:54:43,998
It's going to make for one complicated
relationship between you and I.

785
00:54:51,440 --> 00:54:57,300
In case you're curious, her father and
I were discussing her marriage to me.

786
00:55:00,600 --> 00:55:01,600
Stop it!

787
00:55:06,140 --> 00:55:07,940
Who do you think you are?

788
00:55:08,240 --> 00:55:12,500
You can't take advantage of
Asuna like this Take advantage?

789
00:55:12,940 --> 00:55:13,877
Oh, please.

790
00:55:13,960 --> 00:55:16,680
If anything, I have a right to her!

791
00:55:17,460 --> 00:55:19,460
Perhaps I should explain why?

792
00:55:21,100 --> 00:55:23,260
Any idea what happened to Argus?

793
00:55:23,840 --> 00:55:26,177
They're the company that developed SAO.

794
00:55:26,260 --> 00:55:28,397
I heard they closed it down.

795
00:55:28,480 --> 00:55:29,600
Very good!

796
00:55:30,300 --> 00:55:33,980
The lawsuits and damages they
had to pay took their toll.

797
00:55:34,500 --> 00:55:36,794
The company was forced into bankruptcy.

798
00:55:37,240 --> 00:55:41,300
But the maintenance of the SAO
servers was given to another company.

799
00:55:41,540 --> 00:55:47,060
An electronics manufacturer, where
Asuna's father, Shozo Yuki, is the CEO.

800
00:55:47,900 --> 00:55:49,120
Wrecked progress.

801
00:55:50,020 --> 00:55:54,120
And I work for the company's
full-dive technology R &D division.

802
00:55:54,820 --> 00:55:57,820
In other words, and without
getting into specifics,

803
00:55:57,980 --> 00:56:01,340
you could say I'm the
one keeping Asuna alive.

804
00:56:02,300 --> 00:56:07,065
Now I ask you, is it wrong for me to expect
a little compensation for my trouble?

805
00:56:08,260 --> 00:56:11,557
I don't know what kind of promises
you made to each other in the game,

806
00:56:11,640 --> 00:56:13,052
and I don't really care.

807
00:56:13,500 --> 00:56:16,960
But I don't ever want to see
you here again. Understood?

808
00:56:17,660 --> 00:56:21,260
And from now on, stay
away from the Yuki family.

809
00:56:21,900 --> 00:56:25,820
We're having the ceremony here
on January 26th, a week from now.

810
00:56:26,500 --> 00:56:27,330
Save the date.

811
00:56:27,800 --> 00:56:31,117
Even though you're not welcome here
anymore, you should come to the wedding.

812
00:56:31,200 --> 00:56:32,520
No need to thank me.

813
00:56:35,240 --> 00:56:36,070
Well, Mr.

814
00:56:36,153 --> 00:56:38,846
Hero, you've got the
room all to yourself now.

815
00:56:39,400 --> 00:56:40,812
Say goodbye and get out.

816
00:56:47,680 --> 00:56:48,510
Jeez.

817
00:56:48,920 --> 00:56:49,750
Geez.

818
00:56:49,833 --> 00:56:51,337
Didn't you think he was
suspicious after that?

819
00:56:51,420 --> 00:56:54,126
No, because all I could
think about was Asuna.

820
00:56:54,320 --> 00:56:57,677
Then a friend showed me a screenshot
with an avatar that looked like her,

821
00:56:57,760 --> 00:56:59,289
but that was my only clue.

822
00:56:59,420 --> 00:57:03,120
And based on that, you dove
into ALO to try and save her?

823
00:57:03,400 --> 00:57:06,940
Well, it was all I had to go
on, and that was enough for me.

824
00:57:10,360 --> 00:57:11,817
I need your help again.

825
00:57:11,900 --> 00:57:12,980
One more time.

826
00:57:24,640 --> 00:57:26,100
Link, start!

827
00:58:07,380 --> 00:58:13,240
I'm back in another game, even after
everything I just went through.

828
00:58:18,160 --> 00:58:18,990
Ugh!

829
00:58:19,440 --> 00:58:20,270
Ugh!

830
00:58:26,160 --> 00:58:26,990
Oh!

831
00:58:31,160 --> 00:58:31,990
Oh! Huh?

832
00:58:49,100 --> 00:58:49,930
Hey, Yui.

833
00:58:50,013 --> 00:58:50,843
It's me.

834
00:58:51,200 --> 00:58:52,100
You remember?

835
00:58:56,420 --> 00:58:57,440
I do.

836
00:58:57,740 --> 00:58:59,400
I remember you, Daddy.

837
00:59:01,700 --> 00:59:02,530
Yui!

838
00:59:07,260 --> 00:59:09,540
Daddy! Daddy! Daddy!

839
00:59:12,200 --> 00:59:13,380
You're back.

840
00:59:13,620 --> 00:59:14,540
It's a miracle.

841
00:59:17,060 --> 00:59:18,140
Listen, Yui.

842
00:59:18,600 --> 00:59:22,460
I think your mommy might
be stuck in here somewhere.

843
00:59:23,040 --> 00:59:24,200
Mommy? Really?

844
00:59:24,540 --> 00:59:26,246
What do you mean she's stuck?

845
00:59:27,520 --> 00:59:31,500
After SAO was cleared, Asuna
never woke up in the real world.

846
00:59:32,200 --> 00:59:34,420
I found out she was seen in Alfheim.

847
00:59:34,640 --> 00:59:37,405
There's a picture, but
it's too blurry to tell.

848
00:59:37,820 --> 00:59:39,320
What are we going to do?

849
00:59:41,780 --> 00:59:44,160
What are you doing? Go! Get out of here!

850
00:59:44,680 --> 00:59:48,497
Would someone tell me why three big
guys are fighting one single girl?

851
00:59:48,580 --> 00:59:50,639
That's pretty uncool if you ask me.

852
00:59:50,840 --> 00:59:51,840
What did you say?

853
00:59:52,180 --> 00:59:54,297
You better get your ass out of here, noob.

854
00:59:54,380 --> 00:59:55,210
Fast!

855
00:59:57,100 --> 01:00:02,100
Now, if I remember correctly, the player
called Leafa is your younger sister, right?

856
01:00:02,920 --> 01:00:08,360
Yeah, she's the last person I ever expected
to run into an ALO, especially that way.

857
01:00:18,580 --> 01:00:19,620
No way!

858
01:00:19,880 --> 01:00:22,117
You just swam 25 meters
like it was nothing!

859
01:00:22,200 --> 01:00:24,729
You even got your
breathing technique down.

860
01:00:26,040 --> 01:00:27,687
You got the hang of it fast.

861
01:00:27,940 --> 01:00:29,293
You are a good athlete.

862
01:00:29,400 --> 01:00:31,047
It's all thanks to you guys.

863
01:00:32,620 --> 01:00:33,450
What's up?

864
01:00:33,533 --> 01:00:36,337
Are you starting to miss your
big brother or something?

865
01:00:36,420 --> 01:00:37,540
No, not at all.

866
01:00:37,740 --> 01:00:40,180
I was just wondering why he's so late.

867
01:00:40,600 --> 01:00:44,365
I don't have a brother or sister,
but I always wished I had one.

868
01:00:44,460 --> 01:00:46,897
Being close with him is nothing
to be embarrassed about.

869
01:00:46,980 --> 01:00:49,160
You think so? Mm-hmm.

870
01:00:50,800 --> 01:00:54,300
Well, the thing is, before
he got trapped inside SAO,

871
01:00:54,500 --> 01:00:56,441
we weren't really all that close.

872
01:00:57,000 --> 01:01:01,353
I wanted to see what those VR Miss he
was so obsessed with were all about.

873
01:01:01,720 --> 01:01:03,740
That's why I started playing ALO.

874
01:01:04,340 --> 01:01:06,928
He's the reason I'm
such a badass gamer now.

875
01:01:08,140 --> 01:01:12,337
Kirito said he needed help getting to the
World Tree, and you showed him the way.

876
01:01:12,420 --> 01:01:16,714
Yeah, but when I first met him in
there, I had no idea he was my brother.

877
01:01:17,100 --> 01:01:19,880
He came off like just
another obnoxious gamer.

878
01:01:20,800 --> 01:01:24,797
I kind of thought he was a dork, because
sometimes he'd get all broody and emo.

879
01:01:24,880 --> 01:01:27,037
But the weird thing is, I hung around.

880
01:01:27,120 --> 01:01:29,120
I don't know why I did, but I did.

881
01:01:29,920 --> 01:01:30,750
Daddy?

882
01:01:32,400 --> 01:01:33,230
Sorry.

883
01:01:33,420 --> 01:01:37,832
It's just that I have to get to the
top of the world tree as soon as I can.

884
01:01:40,160 --> 01:01:41,620
Okay, what's the rush?

885
01:01:41,900 --> 01:01:44,200
I'm sort of looking for someone.

886
01:01:44,780 --> 01:01:45,780
What do you mean?

887
01:01:46,760 --> 01:01:49,360
No offense, but it's hard to explain.

888
01:01:56,260 --> 01:01:57,340
Thank you, Leafa.

889
01:01:58,000 --> 01:02:00,882
All the info you gave me
is really going to help.

890
01:02:06,860 --> 01:02:07,690
Wait.

891
01:02:07,900 --> 01:02:10,547
Are you heading for the
World Tree right now?

892
01:02:11,280 --> 01:02:12,110
Uh-huh.

893
01:02:12,440 --> 01:02:13,911
I need to see for myself.

894
01:02:16,620 --> 01:02:20,357
Alone that's crazy it's
really far away and

895
01:02:20,440 --> 01:02:22,852
you'll have to fight a bunch of monsters.

896
01:02:23,020 --> 01:02:25,079
I know you can handle yourself but.

897
01:02:28,300 --> 01:02:30,540
Hey if you want i can take you there.

898
01:02:33,900 --> 01:02:36,377
The world tree was way far i can't believe

899
01:02:36,460 --> 01:02:39,100
we made it in three
days it was crazy tough.

900
01:02:39,760 --> 01:02:41,737
Thank you for helping him, Tsukaha.

901
01:02:41,820 --> 01:02:43,644
No, you don't have to thank me.

902
01:02:43,940 --> 01:02:45,360
I actually had a blast.

903
01:02:45,840 --> 01:02:49,840
It was tough, but it was fun
going on an adventure with Kirito.

904
01:02:53,100 --> 01:02:54,688
Hey, you getting tired yet?

905
01:02:54,880 --> 01:02:56,380
No, I'm good to go.

906
01:02:56,540 --> 01:02:57,980
Okay, Mr. Tough Guy.

907
01:02:58,280 --> 01:03:02,697
I hate to break it to you, but flying's
out for both of us for a little while.

908
01:03:02,780 --> 01:03:03,780
Huh? How come?

909
01:03:03,960 --> 01:03:06,136
You see that mountain way over there?

910
01:03:06,300 --> 01:03:09,017
It's above the altitude
limit, so we can't fly over.

911
01:03:09,100 --> 01:03:12,357
The only way anyone can pass
it is to go through the caves.

912
01:03:12,440 --> 01:03:15,957
It's the toughest part of the trip
between Sylph Territory and Arun.

913
01:03:16,040 --> 01:03:17,060
Or so I've heard.

914
01:03:17,420 --> 01:03:19,596
I've never even been this far myself.

915
01:03:19,840 --> 01:03:20,740
Guess we walk.

916
01:03:21,280 --> 01:03:24,160
These caves, are they long? Pretty long.

917
01:03:24,660 --> 01:03:26,537
There's a mining town about halfway.

918
01:03:26,620 --> 01:03:28,977
It's neutral territory,
so we can rest there.

919
01:03:29,060 --> 01:03:30,080
That reminds me.

920
01:03:30,260 --> 01:03:32,277
Are you good for time, or
do you have to get back?

921
01:03:32,360 --> 01:03:34,595
It's seven at night in the real world.

922
01:03:34,840 --> 01:03:36,577
Yeah, I can keep going for a while.

923
01:03:36,660 --> 01:03:37,490
Cool.

924
01:03:37,573 --> 01:03:39,017
I can too, so let's keep going.

925
01:03:39,100 --> 01:03:41,577
But since we're here,
we should rotate out.

926
01:03:41,660 --> 01:03:43,140
Wait, rotate? Yeah.

927
01:03:43,620 --> 01:03:46,917
We take turns logging out and
resting while the other keeps watch.

928
01:03:47,000 --> 01:03:49,457
You can't log out when you're
in the field, remember?

929
01:03:49,540 --> 01:03:51,597
So we have to take turns logging out.

930
01:03:51,680 --> 01:03:54,817
The person who stays behind
guards the other's avatar.

931
01:03:54,900 --> 01:03:56,371
Okay, sounds like a plan.

932
01:03:56,960 --> 01:03:57,790
Ladies first.

933
01:04:13,120 --> 01:04:15,100
I can't wait to get back there.

934
01:04:28,080 --> 01:04:28,910
Kirito...

935
01:04:29,940 --> 01:04:32,657
It's not that I'm in love
with him or anything,

936
01:04:32,740 --> 01:04:35,681
or that I've got someone
to go on adventures with.

937
01:04:36,560 --> 01:04:40,080
No, I'm just excited I get
to go places in a new world.

938
01:04:49,760 --> 01:04:51,757
So, what'd you think of him after that?

939
01:04:51,840 --> 01:04:53,857
You still didn't know who he was, right?

940
01:04:53,940 --> 01:04:56,116
Did you think he was awesome or what?

941
01:04:56,300 --> 01:04:58,000
I don't know about awesome.

942
01:04:58,360 --> 01:05:01,097
I guess, if anything, I
thought he was really fast.

943
01:05:01,180 --> 01:05:03,997
Later on, I saw how focused
he was during battle,

944
01:05:04,080 --> 01:05:06,551
Way more than anyone I'd ever seen before.

945
01:05:06,640 --> 01:05:08,000
That's enough, Kirito!

946
01:05:08,260 --> 01:05:11,437
If we lose, it'll just mean a
couple extra hours of flying!

947
01:05:11,520 --> 01:05:13,108
Let's give up while we can!

948
01:05:13,800 --> 01:05:14,660
No way.

949
01:05:16,140 --> 01:05:19,846
As long as I'm alive, I'm not
gonna let anyone in my party die.

950
01:05:20,220 --> 01:05:22,080
I won't let that happen again.

951
01:05:39,680 --> 01:05:42,897
What the hell what's he
doing when I realized

952
01:05:42,980 --> 01:05:44,837
why he took those battles so seriously?

953
01:05:44,920 --> 01:05:46,717
Because there was someone he was trying to

954
01:05:46,800 --> 01:05:50,380
protect I thought this is
a guy I can believe in.

955
01:05:53,180 --> 01:05:59,457
It's just a game in the end anything goes
right if you want to kill you kill if

956
01:05:59,540 --> 01:06:05,697
you want to steal you steal a lot of
people think like that more than I care to

957
01:06:05,780 --> 01:06:09,997
know and in a way I get it even I used

958
01:06:10,080 --> 01:06:14,497
to think like that but none of it's true

959
01:06:14,580 --> 01:06:19,460
in a virtual world there's things you have
to protect because it's a virtual world

960
01:06:19,980 --> 01:06:24,937
someone special taught me that
if you give into your impulses

961
01:06:25,020 --> 01:06:28,620
in here it's It's gonna change
who you are in the real world.

962
01:06:29,140 --> 01:06:32,081
The player and the character
are one and the same.

963
01:06:33,280 --> 01:06:35,000
Leafa, you're a good person,

964
01:06:35,960 --> 01:06:37,548
and I wanna be your friend.

965
01:06:38,260 --> 01:06:40,613
So it doesn't matter what the reason is.

966
01:06:40,740 --> 01:06:44,681
There's no way in hell I'd ever
attack a friend for my own benefit.

967
01:06:44,920 --> 01:06:46,567
I couldn't live with myself.

968
01:06:47,220 --> 01:06:49,340
It didn't matter what the odds were.

969
01:06:49,760 --> 01:06:53,777
My brother would never turn his back on
a fight if it was for the right thing.

970
01:06:53,860 --> 01:06:57,560
That's why I knew he could
never lose. Ah! Kirito!

971
01:07:27,720 --> 01:07:28,550
No!

972
01:07:56,280 --> 01:07:59,097
You know, I think it's great
you guys are close and all,

973
01:07:59,180 --> 01:08:02,957
but I get the feeling you're a little
too close, know what I'm saying?

974
01:08:03,040 --> 01:08:04,922
God, what are you talking about?

975
01:08:05,300 --> 01:08:07,377
Anyway, shouldn't I
get back to practicing?

976
01:08:07,460 --> 01:08:08,578
You heard the lady.

977
01:08:08,700 --> 01:08:10,000
Let's get back to it.

978
01:08:16,220 --> 01:08:18,860
If only I'd known before I fell in love.

979
01:08:23,680 --> 01:08:24,660
Is that you?

980
01:08:25,760 --> 01:08:26,720
Kazutou?

981
01:08:27,480 --> 01:08:28,310
Huh?

982
01:08:30,360 --> 01:08:31,190
Sugu?

983
01:08:32,060 --> 01:08:33,180
Suguha?

984
01:08:35,760 --> 01:08:36,920
I can't believe it.

985
01:08:37,340 --> 01:08:38,880
It's not fair!

986
01:08:39,440 --> 01:08:40,270
No!

987
01:08:40,600 --> 01:08:41,520
Sugu!

988
01:08:43,260 --> 01:08:44,380
Sugu!

989
01:08:47,700 --> 01:08:48,737
I...

990
01:08:48,820 --> 01:08:50,120
I...

991
01:08:50,760 --> 01:08:51,660
I...

992
01:08:52,760 --> 01:08:55,100
I betrayed the feelings I had!

993
01:08:55,760 --> 01:08:58,840
I betrayed the love I felt for you.

994
01:08:59,600 --> 01:09:01,020
When I met Kirito,

995
01:09:01,140 --> 01:09:05,257
I thought finally I could give up on
all these feelings I have for you.

996
01:09:05,340 --> 01:09:06,280
What the hell?

997
01:09:06,500 --> 01:09:07,760
I already had!

998
01:09:09,220 --> 01:09:11,897
But now I'm...

999
01:09:11,980 --> 01:09:14,240
Well, I mean love?

1000
01:09:14,440 --> 01:09:15,817
But you and me, we're...

1001
01:09:15,900 --> 01:09:16,760
No, we're not.

1002
01:09:17,340 --> 01:09:19,020
I said no, we're not!

1003
01:09:19,740 --> 01:09:23,269
I know you're not really my
brother and I'm not your sister.

1004
01:09:23,600 --> 01:09:27,100
I've known all along, for
the last two years anyway.

1005
01:09:28,800 --> 01:09:30,857
That's why you quit Kendo, isn't it?

1006
01:09:30,940 --> 01:09:32,822
And why you started avoiding me?

1007
01:09:33,160 --> 01:09:36,042
It's because you knew the
whole time, didn't you?

1008
01:09:36,260 --> 01:09:40,025
You pushed me away because I'm
not your real sister, didn't you?

1009
01:09:40,220 --> 01:09:41,050
You did.

1010
01:09:41,860 --> 01:09:45,154
Well, if that's how it is,
why do you care about me now?

1011
01:09:46,520 --> 01:09:47,480
I just...

1012
01:09:48,140 --> 01:09:52,260
I was so happy you came back from SAO.

1013
01:09:53,120 --> 01:09:58,002
I was happy because you were being nice to
me again, just like when we were little.

1014
01:09:58,420 --> 01:10:01,302
It felt like you were
finally giving me a chance.

1015
01:10:01,560 --> 01:10:02,854
That's what I thought.

1016
01:10:03,960 --> 01:10:09,340
But now, if this is how it is, I wish
you'd kept on being a jerk to me.

1017
01:10:11,440 --> 01:10:15,840
If you had, I wouldn't have
realized how I felt about you.

1018
01:10:16,300 --> 01:10:19,757
I wouldn't have felt sad and
jealous when I found out about her.

1019
01:10:19,840 --> 01:10:21,977
And I wouldn't have tried forgetting about

1020
01:10:22,060 --> 01:10:24,648
you and falling in love
with Kinito instead!

1021
01:10:29,640 --> 01:10:30,780
I'm sorry.

1022
01:10:39,660 --> 01:10:40,677
Go on.

1023
01:10:40,760 --> 01:10:41,940
Leave me alone.

1024
01:10:59,980 --> 01:11:01,380
Oh

1025
01:11:30,980 --> 01:11:32,140
What are you doing?

1026
01:11:32,720 --> 01:11:33,900
What are you doing?

1027
01:11:38,140 --> 01:11:40,120
Look, I wanted to apologize.

1028
01:11:41,540 --> 01:11:44,364
But I just didn't know
how to go about doing it.

1029
01:11:45,280 --> 01:11:47,221
So I was going to throw the duel.

1030
01:11:49,420 --> 01:11:50,360
You were

1031
01:11:53,660 --> 01:11:54,740
I'm sorry

1032
01:11:57,900 --> 01:11:59,160
I'm sorry too

1033
01:12:00,880 --> 01:12:06,100
I think my problem is I never really
came back to the real world after SAO

1034
01:12:06,720 --> 01:12:13,460
and I can't come back until she wakes up
in a way the game hasn't ended for me yet

1035
01:12:14,440 --> 01:12:15,917
and I guess that's why?

1036
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:19,317
I still haven't figured out how
I fit in at home or with you.

1037
01:12:19,400 --> 01:12:20,460
Not yet, anyway.

1038
01:12:23,140 --> 01:12:24,964
And when you do, I'll be there.

1039
01:12:25,140 --> 01:12:27,077
It doesn't matter how long it takes.

1040
01:12:27,160 --> 01:12:30,513
I'll be waiting for the day
you come back to us for real.

1041
01:12:30,740 --> 01:12:33,380
Until then, I'll help you in here.

1042
01:12:43,380 --> 01:12:44,637
Hey, Suguha?

1043
01:12:44,720 --> 01:12:46,977
You won't learn how to
swim unless you practice!

1044
01:12:47,060 --> 01:12:48,900
Yeah, I'm coming.

1045
01:12:50,480 --> 01:12:52,797
Okay, so thanks to your sister's help.

1046
01:12:52,880 --> 01:12:54,497
You finally reached the world tree.

1047
01:12:54,580 --> 01:12:57,157
In the report it says Sugo's grand quest?

1048
01:12:57,240 --> 01:12:59,217
Was designed to be impossible to clear.

1049
01:12:59,300 --> 01:13:01,637
But somehow you cleared it on your own!

1050
01:13:01,720 --> 01:13:03,137
And went on to rescue Asuna.

1051
01:13:03,220 --> 01:13:05,320
No, that's not how it happened.

1052
01:13:05,540 --> 01:13:06,952
I didn't clear it alone.

1053
01:13:08,100 --> 01:13:09,500
I'm almost there!

1054
01:13:33,220 --> 01:13:36,220
Just a little further?

1055
01:13:38,440 --> 01:13:46,790
Ah!

1056
01:13:48,280 --> 01:13:49,110
Cats!

1057
01:13:59,100 --> 01:14:00,500
Cats!

1058
01:14:20,080 --> 01:14:22,880
Outro music

1059
01:14:37,040 --> 01:14:38,017
No way!

1060
01:14:38,100 --> 01:14:40,000
He's using a dark magic spell!

1061
01:14:53,400 --> 01:14:56,880
Okay, Dragoons, get ready
to choke these suckers!

1062
01:14:58,820 --> 01:15:01,526
Stealth warriors, prepare
to engage the enemy!

1063
01:15:02,380 --> 01:15:04,680
Fire breath, attack!

1064
01:15:13,840 --> 01:15:16,280
Fenrir storm, fire at will!

1065
01:15:22,160 --> 01:15:27,400
I cleared the quest, thanks to
Leafa and Recon, Sakuya and Alicia,

1066
01:15:27,740 --> 01:15:30,500
and all the Sylph and Cats warriors.

1067
01:15:31,060 --> 01:15:35,220
If it wasn't for them, I would have
never been able to reach Asuna.

1068
01:15:36,100 --> 01:15:36,930
I see.

1069
01:15:56,140 --> 01:15:58,120
And then Sugo, a .k .a.

1070
01:15:58,240 --> 01:16:00,122
Oberon the Fairy King, appeared.

1071
01:16:00,720 --> 01:16:04,657
Usually I wouldn't think it possible
for a player to beat the Game Master.

1072
01:16:04,740 --> 01:16:06,960
But then, you're an unusual player.

1073
01:16:10,840 --> 01:16:11,670
Yes!

1074
01:16:14,840 --> 01:16:15,670
Great!

1075
01:16:16,880 --> 01:16:17,710
Ha!

1076
01:16:17,793 --> 01:16:18,623
That's what I was hoping for!

1077
01:16:18,706 --> 01:16:21,504
You can't get NPC girls
to make faces like that!

1078
01:16:25,340 --> 01:16:27,300
Ah, you smell lovely.

1079
01:16:28,180 --> 01:16:32,709
Figuring out how to replicate the way
you smell in real life was a challenge.

1080
01:16:33,320 --> 01:16:36,777
And don't even get me
started on how hard it was to

1081
01:16:36,860 --> 01:16:39,940
get an analyzer into your
hospital room undetected.

1082
01:16:40,860 --> 01:16:42,280
Get away from her!

1083
01:16:42,920 --> 01:16:44,100
She's so cool!

1084
01:16:47,960 --> 01:16:49,720
Give me a break.

1085
01:16:49,960 --> 01:16:53,840
Why don't you stay down and
grovel like a good little doggy?

1086
01:16:58,800 --> 01:16:59,630
Cait!

1087
01:17:03,500 --> 01:17:08,840
System command, change the pain
absorber from level 10 to level 8.

1088
01:17:13,400 --> 01:17:14,517
Hurts, doesn't it?

1089
01:17:14,600 --> 01:17:18,953
I'll increase the pain gradually to
give you something to look forward to.

1090
01:17:19,060 --> 01:17:20,040
By the way,

1091
01:17:20,420 --> 01:17:25,302
once it drops below level three, it'll
start affecting your body in the real world.

1092
01:17:25,400 --> 01:17:26,540
As for you...

1093
01:17:42,320 --> 01:17:44,120
Yummy. How sweet.

1094
01:17:45,120 --> 01:17:46,340
Sugou!

1095
01:17:46,540 --> 01:17:47,657
You bastard!

1096
01:17:47,740 --> 01:17:49,480
You BASTARD!

1097
01:17:57,140 --> 01:17:59,940
I'll kill you! You hear?

1098
01:18:00,300 --> 01:18:02,120
I'm gonna kill you!

1099
01:18:14,600 --> 01:18:15,900
Are you giving up?

1100
01:18:16,660 --> 01:18:17,490
No.

1101
01:18:18,040 --> 01:18:19,800
I'm facing reality.

1102
01:18:20,320 --> 01:18:21,820
Then you are giving up.

1103
01:18:22,000 --> 01:18:24,540
To the power of a system you once defied.

1104
01:18:25,400 --> 01:18:27,200
What choice do I have?

1105
01:18:27,420 --> 01:18:28,880
I'm just a player.

1106
01:18:29,160 --> 01:18:30,720
And he's the GM.

1107
01:18:31,540 --> 01:18:34,600
Then our battle was... What? A joke?

1108
01:18:35,500 --> 01:18:37,877
Do you remember how
you showed me the power

1109
01:18:37,960 --> 01:18:40,607
of the human will was
superior to the system?

1110
01:18:40,840 --> 01:18:43,781
How you showed me the
possibilities of the future?

1111
01:18:44,420 --> 01:18:45,250
You're...

1112
01:18:47,300 --> 01:18:49,760
Get up, Kirito. Get up!

1113
01:18:52,420 --> 01:18:55,538
GMs are the supreme rulers
of the worlds they create.

1114
01:18:55,920 --> 01:18:58,017
And as long as they're in that world,

1115
01:18:58,100 --> 01:19:00,982
they can access the powers
of a god if they want.

1116
01:19:01,560 --> 01:19:04,972
The thing is, it's the system
that gives them their power.

1117
01:19:06,200 --> 01:19:08,729
It's not something they
had to win or hone.

1118
01:19:09,540 --> 01:19:12,960
But real power is something
that's only found in you.

1119
01:19:14,120 --> 01:19:17,760
That's true in the virtual
world, and the real one.

1120
01:19:21,580 --> 01:19:23,462
You wanna go get some ice cream?

1121
01:19:23,800 --> 01:19:25,280
Sounds ice, am I right?

1122
01:19:29,480 --> 01:19:32,600
In the end, Sugo overestimated
the power he got.

1123
01:19:33,040 --> 01:19:34,860
That's why he self-destructed.

1124
01:19:35,400 --> 01:19:36,420
That he did.

1125
01:19:36,680 --> 01:19:37,660
That he did.

1126
01:19:47,140 --> 01:19:51,552
As for what happened next, you know
everything there is to know about that.

1127
01:19:51,820 --> 01:19:53,040
I better get going.

1128
01:19:53,640 --> 01:19:56,577
I'm supposed to meet the
others in ALO after this.

1129
01:19:56,660 --> 01:19:58,072
I don't want to be late.

1130
01:19:59,160 --> 01:20:01,513
Before you go, I have one more question.

1131
01:20:02,920 --> 01:20:05,273
I heard about something called the Seed.

1132
01:20:05,500 --> 01:20:06,860
Have you heard of it?

1133
01:20:07,380 --> 01:20:08,840
Yeah, of course.

1134
01:20:16,080 --> 01:20:18,460
See you around, Kirito.

1135
01:20:29,120 --> 01:20:31,180
You know what, Kirito?

1136
01:20:31,380 --> 01:20:33,737
I never appreciated the difference between

1137
01:20:33,820 --> 01:20:37,300
in-game time and real-world
time as I do now. Why?

1138
01:20:37,420 --> 01:20:39,037
Because it's night IRL right now?

1139
01:20:39,120 --> 01:20:41,477
No, because it's a perfect
day at the beach here!

1140
01:20:41,560 --> 01:20:42,697
Those blue skies!

1141
01:20:42,780 --> 01:20:48,480
and that white sand, and those gentle
waves, and that warm sun, and that view.

1142
01:20:50,740 --> 01:20:51,720
What's up, dogs?

1143
01:20:51,900 --> 01:20:52,782
Sorry I'm late.

1144
01:20:54,140 --> 01:20:54,970
What?

1145
01:20:55,053 --> 01:20:56,804
You got a problem with my suit?

1146
01:20:57,000 --> 01:20:59,480
Oh, no, it's the incoming wave!

1147
01:21:00,620 --> 01:21:02,900
We are multiple feet ahead!

1148
01:21:04,180 --> 01:21:05,420
I'll get you back!

1149
01:21:05,840 --> 01:21:07,840
Pain, show her your water breath!

1150
01:21:12,780 --> 01:21:13,720
Higher at will!

1151
01:21:20,820 --> 01:21:22,740
Behold, the power of Rita!

1152
01:21:23,020 --> 01:21:24,373
She's taking care good!

1153
01:21:34,340 --> 01:21:37,520
Leafa, you gonna be okay or
do you need more practice?

1154
01:21:37,960 --> 01:21:39,320
No, I'm good to go.

1155
01:21:39,520 --> 01:21:40,737
I'm not afraid anymore.

1156
01:21:40,820 --> 01:21:43,357
or as long as I can touch the bottom.

1157
01:21:43,440 --> 01:21:44,977
Well, you look more confident.

1158
01:21:45,060 --> 01:21:47,060
Oh, about where we're going today.

1159
01:21:47,440 --> 01:21:52,280
Yeah, I was gonna ask you, any idea how
far under this dungeon's supposed to be?

1160
01:21:52,520 --> 01:21:53,580
Pretty far down.

1161
01:21:53,880 --> 01:21:56,645
I think I heard it was
around a hundred meters.

1162
01:21:56,760 --> 01:21:57,660
A hundred?

1163
01:21:59,920 --> 01:22:02,020
I'm okay, I can do this.

1164
01:22:03,700 --> 01:22:05,520
It's for Yui, after all.

1165
01:22:07,100 --> 01:22:08,960
Thanks a lot, Leafa.

1166
01:22:12,540 --> 01:22:16,837
And then, the second Kirito saw the king
of all fish come storming out of the lake,

1167
01:22:16,920 --> 01:22:18,300
he screamed so loud!

1168
01:22:18,680 --> 01:22:19,780
Oh, ahhh!

1169
01:22:20,580 --> 01:22:22,600
Come on, you're so exaggerating.

1170
01:22:23,220 --> 01:22:26,060
I went, whoa, but that's
about as loud as I got.

1171
01:22:27,720 --> 01:22:30,896
Lucky, I wish I could have
seen the king of fish, too.

1172
01:22:31,260 --> 01:22:34,495
Don't worry, once the new
Aincrad opens up on floor 22,

1173
01:22:34,600 --> 01:22:38,718
we're going to buy another cabin and
have another contest at the lake.

1174
01:22:38,900 --> 01:22:39,997
Wait till you see it.

1175
01:22:40,080 --> 01:22:42,820
That fish is so ginormous, it's scary.

1176
01:22:43,580 --> 01:22:45,180
So scary, you might cry.

1177
01:22:45,360 --> 01:22:46,460
Oh, no I won't!

1178
01:22:46,620 --> 01:22:49,417
You say it's big, but when you
factor in the area of the lake,

1179
01:22:49,500 --> 01:22:52,377
it can't possibly be as big
as a whale in the real world!

1180
01:22:52,460 --> 01:22:54,813
Wait, have you seen a real whale before?

1181
01:22:54,940 --> 01:23:00,060
No, I just estimated the size of one
using measurements and video data I found.

1182
01:23:00,380 --> 01:23:03,321
I wish I could see real
world things like you two,

1183
01:23:03,420 --> 01:23:06,655
but since I can't, I just
have to make do with my data.

1184
01:23:07,140 --> 01:23:07,970
I see.

1185
01:23:08,140 --> 01:23:09,280
You poor thing.

1186
01:23:10,080 --> 01:23:12,080
If only Alfheim had whales.

1187
01:23:12,360 --> 01:23:14,277
I know you'd get a kick out of them.

1188
01:23:14,360 --> 01:23:15,980
They really are gigantic.

1189
01:23:16,360 --> 01:23:19,977
They jump out of the ocean and land
with a big splash and - Hold the phone!

1190
01:23:20,060 --> 01:23:21,140
What is it?

1191
01:23:21,640 --> 01:23:24,340
I just remembered something. That's right.

1192
01:23:24,580 --> 01:23:29,462
In the south of Sylph Territory, there's
supposed to be a quest with a whale in it.

1193
01:23:29,820 --> 01:23:30,820
Oh, can we go?

1194
01:23:31,060 --> 01:23:33,825
If we went, then maybe
I'd get to ride a whale.

1195
01:23:34,900 --> 01:23:36,782
That's probably not a good idea.

1196
01:23:38,440 --> 01:23:42,220
Hey, Kirito, you absolutely 100
% sure this quest is for real?

1197
01:23:42,440 --> 01:23:45,597
Because if not, man, you're
going to break Yui's heart.

1198
01:23:45,680 --> 01:23:48,397
If it turns out to be a
jellyfish or a sea butterfly,

1199
01:23:48,480 --> 01:23:50,421
it's going to be lamer than hell.

1200
01:23:50,560 --> 01:23:54,520
If it's a giant sea butterfly,
that would still be pretty rad.

1201
01:23:55,100 --> 01:23:56,837
You find anything on it, Eggiel?

1202
01:23:56,920 --> 01:23:57,750
Not much.

1203
01:23:57,833 --> 01:24:00,217
The quest's way out on
the edge of the world map.

1204
01:24:00,300 --> 01:24:03,117
I tried, man, but there's not a whole
lot of people who know about it.

1205
01:24:03,200 --> 01:24:06,357
Only thing I could confirm
is the part about a big-ass

1206
01:24:06,440 --> 01:24:10,497
sea monster showing up at the
end that's all so at least

1207
01:24:10,580 --> 01:24:14,117
we got something to look
forward to come on let's hit

1208
01:24:14,200 --> 01:24:18,840
this hey guys it's time we
start saddling up for the quest

1209
01:24:19,480 --> 01:24:20,310
okay

1210
01:24:39,340 --> 01:24:43,000
Oh, uh, are you going to
wear your armor on the quest?

1211
01:24:43,240 --> 01:24:44,122
Duh, of course.

1212
01:24:44,320 --> 01:24:45,677
We are going into battle.

1213
01:24:45,760 --> 01:24:48,525
Hurry up and change and
we'll leave you behind.

1214
01:24:52,560 --> 01:24:53,437
Okay, so...

1215
01:24:53,520 --> 01:24:56,937
If you guys don't mind, I'd like
to be the party leader for today.

1216
01:24:57,020 --> 01:24:58,557
You all know our objective,

1217
01:24:58,640 --> 01:25:02,640
so if anyone sees a whale out there,
call it out and follow my lead.

1218
01:25:03,380 --> 01:25:04,380
Thanks, you guys.

1219
01:25:04,520 --> 01:25:06,820
I really appreciate this. Okay, then.

1220
01:25:07,020 --> 01:25:08,460
You ready? Yeah!

1221
01:25:24,820 --> 01:25:27,761
According to these
coordinates, it should be here.

1222
01:25:27,920 --> 01:25:29,508
Hey, is that it over there?

1223
01:25:33,700 --> 01:25:37,347
Okay, everyone, I'm gonna cast
a water-breathing spell for us.

1224
01:26:02,080 --> 01:26:03,220
Ah! What?

1225
01:26:11,100 --> 01:26:11,930
Lima!

1226
01:26:32,940 --> 01:26:34,340
Wow, look at that!

1227
01:26:34,700 --> 01:26:37,060
Hey, I think I see someone down there.

1228
01:26:40,480 --> 01:26:43,160
Nice, we got an NPC waiting for us.

1229
01:26:43,380 --> 01:26:47,439
Dude, if we're on an undersea quest,
then I bet that NPC's a mermaid!

1230
01:26:47,880 --> 01:26:49,800
Don't worry, Miss Mermaid!

1231
01:26:50,080 --> 01:26:51,900
Klein's coming to save you!

1232
01:26:54,720 --> 01:26:56,300
Here I am, my lady.

1233
01:26:56,640 --> 01:26:58,060
My name's...

1234
01:27:00,780 --> 01:27:02,120
That's not a mermaid.

1235
01:27:02,380 --> 01:27:03,380
That's a grandpa.

1236
01:27:04,780 --> 01:27:06,898
Let's see what this gentleman wants.

1237
01:27:13,080 --> 01:27:15,800
Greetings, fairies from the surface world.

1238
01:27:16,100 --> 01:27:19,041
Could you possibly help
an old man with a dilemma?

1239
01:27:25,380 --> 01:27:26,977
Is something wrong, Leafa?

1240
01:27:27,060 --> 01:27:28,740
Oh, no.

1241
01:27:29,060 --> 01:27:31,060
I just noticed the old man's name.

1242
01:27:31,240 --> 01:27:33,017
I think I've seen it somewhere before.

1243
01:27:33,100 --> 01:27:37,880
Some thieves have stolen a present I
acquired for an old friend of mine.

1244
01:27:38,380 --> 01:27:40,640
The temple behind me is their hideout.

1245
01:27:41,080 --> 01:27:44,727
Could you please retrieve it for
me before the rascals return?

1246
01:27:45,160 --> 01:27:46,640
We'd be happy to help.

1247
01:27:46,920 --> 01:27:49,220
I am most grateful, kind fairy.

1248
01:27:49,880 --> 01:27:54,537
The item in question is a pearl
about this size. Cha-ching!

1249
01:27:54,620 --> 01:27:57,657
I hope you're not thinking
about swiping it and selling it.

1250
01:27:57,740 --> 01:27:59,820
No, not this time, anyway.

1251
01:28:00,260 --> 01:28:03,240
I'm counting on you, my noble fairies.

1252
01:28:03,380 --> 01:28:08,560
If you succeed in retrieving the
pearl, I will reward you handsomely.

1253
01:28:11,200 --> 01:28:14,740
Okay, so it looks like this
will be a search and seize.

1254
01:28:15,060 --> 01:28:17,977
But there might be monsters
in there, so stay sharp.

1255
01:28:18,060 --> 01:28:19,557
If you're in the vanguard,

1256
01:28:19,640 --> 01:28:22,737
your sword strokes will be slower
underwater, so compensate for that.

1257
01:28:22,820 --> 01:28:27,320
And rearguard, don't even think about
using any lightning spells. Right!

1258
01:28:29,560 --> 01:28:31,780
Okay, guys, let's move out.

1259
01:28:51,600 --> 01:28:56,080
Hey, uh, Kirito, I don't think Leafa's
cool with this underwater stuff.

1260
01:28:56,560 --> 01:28:59,057
Shouldn't you, like, keep a
closer eye on her or something?

1261
01:28:59,140 --> 01:28:59,970
You okay?

1262
01:29:00,240 --> 01:29:01,946
Yeah, you're right, I should.

1263
01:29:02,180 --> 01:29:04,080
But it's so weird between us.

1264
01:29:04,260 --> 01:29:06,517
If it's just her and
me, everything's cool.

1265
01:29:06,600 --> 01:29:09,337
But if we're in a party
together, it's crazy awkward.

1266
01:29:09,420 --> 01:29:10,577
What are you talking about?

1267
01:29:10,660 --> 01:29:11,719
She's your sister.

1268
01:29:11,960 --> 01:29:14,677
All you have to do is be
yourself and look out for her.

1269
01:29:14,760 --> 01:29:16,117
You know, like a big brother.

1270
01:29:16,200 --> 01:29:17,030
I know.

1271
01:29:17,240 --> 01:29:20,652
But when I first met her
in-game, I didn't even realize...

1272
01:29:26,360 --> 01:29:29,419
Yo, you gotta be straight
up blind to miss that pit.

1273
01:29:29,720 --> 01:29:30,580
Dumb asses.

1274
01:29:30,700 --> 01:29:33,817
I can't believe he used to be a
top player in the assault team.

1275
01:29:33,900 --> 01:29:34,997
It doesn't matter to me.

1276
01:29:35,080 --> 01:29:37,668
I think he's rad no
matter how clumsy he is.

1277
01:29:40,880 --> 01:29:42,380
Daddy, in front of you!

1278
01:29:45,280 --> 01:29:46,380
Is that the whale?

1279
01:29:46,940 --> 01:29:47,770
No.

1280
01:29:48,320 --> 01:29:49,680
Not even close.

1281
01:29:51,060 --> 01:29:51,890
Attack!

1282
01:29:57,300 --> 01:29:59,006
The head doesn't take damage.

1283
01:29:59,720 --> 01:30:00,779
I'll keep it busy!

1284
01:30:01,480 --> 01:30:04,660
You guys attack its flakes!
Aim on it! Copy that!

1285
01:30:06,840 --> 01:30:08,840
Come on, let's go help them. Okay.

1286
01:30:11,100 --> 01:30:11,930
I'm going.

1287
01:30:14,120 --> 01:30:14,950
Leafa!

1288
01:30:15,033 --> 01:30:17,587
Stay back with Asuna
and hit it with spells!

1289
01:30:22,360 --> 01:30:25,420
After everyone went to all
that trouble coaching me.

1290
01:30:28,120 --> 01:30:29,414
Thanks a bunch, Leafa!

1291
01:30:38,020 --> 01:30:40,060
What am I doing standing here?

1292
01:30:40,280 --> 01:30:42,515
I said I'd follow my brother anywhere!

1293
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:47,260
Leafa, I'll be fine, I can do this!

1294
01:31:04,020 --> 01:31:04,850
Lisa!

1295
01:31:05,180 --> 01:31:07,040
Kirito! Do something!

1296
01:31:17,300 --> 01:31:19,060
Kirito! What are you doing?

1297
01:31:24,540 --> 01:31:27,060
Hey! Ah!

1298
01:32:10,780 --> 01:32:15,457
Oh yeah, when I was little,
I fell into a pond. And...

1299
01:32:15,540 --> 01:32:18,157
I remember sinking...

1300
01:32:18,240 --> 01:32:19,280
and then...

1301
01:32:31,280 --> 01:32:32,110
Sugou!

1302
01:32:33,840 --> 01:32:35,160
Asada!

1303
01:32:41,280 --> 01:32:42,280
I got you!

1304
01:32:45,280 --> 01:32:46,110
Ah!

1305
01:32:50,780 --> 01:32:53,480
Kazuto, you saved me again.

1306
01:33:32,580 --> 01:33:33,580
Oh, man.

1307
01:33:33,940 --> 01:33:37,617
I don't care if I never see another
stupid shrimp or crab again.

1308
01:33:37,700 --> 01:33:38,994
Or a squid or octopus.

1309
01:33:40,680 --> 01:33:44,380
After all that, we never did
get to see a whale. That sucks.

1310
01:33:45,280 --> 01:33:46,110
Yeah, maybe.

1311
01:33:46,460 --> 01:33:48,897
But Yui sure looked
like she was having fun.

1312
01:33:48,980 --> 01:33:49,810
Here you go.

1313
01:33:50,200 --> 01:33:51,760
We got it back for you.

1314
01:33:52,300 --> 01:33:53,130
Thank you.

1315
01:33:53,480 --> 01:33:55,140
This is wonderful.

1316
01:33:55,680 --> 01:33:57,777
Anyone else think it's
weird that we never saw

1317
01:33:57,860 --> 01:34:00,448
those thieves the old
man was talking about?

1318
01:34:00,680 --> 01:34:01,510
Yeah.

1319
01:34:05,360 --> 01:34:06,920
No! Don't give it to him!

1320
01:34:09,020 --> 01:34:09,850
What?

1321
01:34:15,280 --> 01:34:17,620
Look, it's not a pearl, it's an egg.

1322
01:34:18,000 --> 01:34:19,040
What the hell?

1323
01:34:20,440 --> 01:34:22,028
Plunderers of the deep sea.

1324
01:34:23,120 --> 01:34:25,220
Hold on, does that mean us?

1325
01:34:26,820 --> 01:34:30,340
If you don't mind, I'll
take possession of that.

1326
01:34:32,980 --> 01:34:37,100
If you won't hand it over,
you'll leave me no choice.

1327
01:34:58,140 --> 01:34:58,970
Kraken!

1328
01:34:59,080 --> 01:35:01,139
The sea demon from Norse mythology!

1329
01:35:01,580 --> 01:35:04,540
A thousand thanks, my little fairies.

1330
01:35:04,740 --> 01:35:07,800
You have retrieved the
egg of the royal child.

1331
01:35:08,120 --> 01:35:11,532
If not for the magic barrier,
I would have done it myself.

1332
01:35:11,840 --> 01:35:14,340
Now then, hand it over immediately.

1333
01:35:15,280 --> 01:35:16,320
You old coot.

1334
01:35:16,540 --> 01:35:17,540
We will not.

1335
01:35:17,820 --> 01:35:20,617
We're going to put the egg
right back where we found it.

1336
01:35:20,700 --> 01:35:26,700
In that case, you little pests, prepare
to spend eternity in a watery grave.

1337
01:35:41,540 --> 01:35:42,400
Look out!

1338
01:35:45,440 --> 01:35:46,270
Ahhhh!

1339
01:35:56,940 --> 01:36:00,320
Daddy, the stats of that
octopus are unbelievably high!

1340
01:36:00,620 --> 01:36:05,561
I don't think there's a single floor boss
in New Aincrad with stats as high as that.

1341
01:36:20,040 --> 01:36:21,960
I know that spear.

1342
01:36:37,140 --> 01:36:39,900
It's been a long time, old friend.

1343
01:36:40,300 --> 01:36:42,957
I see you're still up to your old tricks.

1344
01:36:43,040 --> 01:36:47,160
And I see you are still playing
lapdog to the minions of Aesir.

1345
01:36:47,440 --> 01:36:50,940
You disgrace your title, Lord of the Sea.

1346
01:36:51,220 --> 01:36:56,060
I am Lord of the Sea, and
you are in my backyard.

1347
01:36:56,740 --> 01:37:01,340
Now, do you really wish to
fight me, Lord of the Abyss?

1348
01:37:04,040 --> 01:37:08,760
I shall withdraw for now,
but take heed, old friend.

1349
01:37:09,140 --> 01:37:10,780
This is not over.

1350
01:37:11,360 --> 01:37:14,540
Soon, I shall claim
the power of the child.

1351
01:37:14,900 --> 01:37:17,620
Then I will rise up against Aesir.

1352
01:37:18,060 --> 01:37:19,600
Mark my words!

1353
01:37:23,480 --> 01:37:28,600
That is the egg of the one who will
someday rule over the seas and the sky.

1354
01:37:29,180 --> 01:37:34,160
I shall take it to a new resting place
where it will be safe from treachery.

1355
01:37:41,700 --> 01:37:44,480
Okay, what the hell's
going on? Is that it?

1356
01:37:44,660 --> 01:37:45,836
We clear it or what?

1357
01:37:46,060 --> 01:37:47,200
I'm lost too.

1358
01:37:47,500 --> 01:37:50,877
Does anyone know what the big guy
and the octopus were talking about?

1359
01:37:50,960 --> 01:37:52,320
It was not important.

1360
01:37:53,040 --> 01:37:58,120
Now, my noble fairies, I shall
transport you back to your own world.

1361
01:37:58,460 --> 01:38:00,520
Um, what do you mean by transport?

1362
01:38:18,940 --> 01:38:22,200
Hey, Peeta, isn't this whale gigantic?

1363
01:38:41,400 --> 01:38:42,230
Oh, yeah!

1364
01:38:42,313 --> 01:38:43,143
and

1365
01:38:43,226 --> 01:38:49,080
I'll

1366
01:39:08,320 --> 01:39:11,160
keep my mind

1367
01:39:58,980 --> 01:40:01,217
I'll see you

1368
01:40:01,300 --> 01:40:08,300
next

1369
01:40:11,080 --> 01:40:11,910
time.

1370
01:40:20,260 --> 01:40:23,980
Thank you so much for your
love and love. Thank you.

1371
01:40:41,160 --> 01:40:41,990
Thank you.
